Z||000000||artherd||11-20-2001||12:48 AM||||I have a friend with a 1967 mustang with a 351W engine (the same as used in the GT350...) bored .030" over, for a 357 ;)<P>He is long on power, but short on traction... (crappy rotting scary 14" evilness.)<P>Well, the subject sells it, I need a complete set of wheels and tyres from/for a 2001 Bullett Mustang.  Tyres need to be grippy 245/45/17(stock size) and not suck.  No warranty kind :)<P>The wheels are 17x8 and need to be OE Ford parts, not fakes.<P>Help me find him the cheapest price we can get, I am worried about him, he has really crappy 14" *hard* slipry rubber on the car now.  It burns through 4th gear, even (mostly) when he doesn't want to.  He's going to get himself killed.<P>Best price I have been able to find (with a set of BFG G-force TAs) is $1,195.00. <P>'take-offs' or slightly used wheels are ok, but new everything vastly perfered.<P>Help me and the Tire Fairy out!!!<P>Here's a pic:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.karkraft.com/bullitt_wheel_and_tire.JPG"> <P><BR>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
